ZVSE2

; Combat_BattleShadows example. Put this file into the Data\s folder of your mod.
; The plugin removes the old shadows by itself every time the MM0 trigger starts again.

; Example 1 (on): shadow around the hex under the mouse.
;   P(hex)/(radius)/(contour): radius 0..4, 0 = only the mouse hex; contour 1 = blinking blue outline.
!?MM0;
!!MM:D?(hex:y);                                   [hex under the mouse]
!!FU(BattleShadow_Radius):P(hex)/1/1;

; Example 2 (off): free shape, up to 10 hexes. -1 = empty slot. The 11th value is the contour switch.
; To turn it on, replace the first character * with ! on the next two lines.
; If both examples are on, both shapes are shown together.
*?MM0;
*!FU(BattleShadow_Hexes):P52/53/54/71/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/1;

; Diagnostics (off): shows the plugin state in the battle hint line instead of the normal hint.
; To turn it on, replace the first character * with ! on the next two lines.
*!FU(BattleShadow_Debug):P?y20/?y21/?y22/?y23/?y24/?y25/?y26/?y27/?y28;
*!MM:M^v%y20 mine=%y21 inList=%y22 list=%y23 noShade=%y24 option=%y25 updates=%y26 anchor=%y27 cursor=%y28^;
